1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,638
An 850 watt power supply doesn't use 850 watts.

2
00:00:05,918 --> 00:00:07,959
Here's what that number really means.

3
00:00:08,709 --> 00:00:11,556
The wattage on a power supply is a maximum.

4
00:00:11,836 --> 00:00:15,854
It's the most it can safely deliver, not what it draws all the time.

5
00:00:16,604 --> 00:00:18,691
Your parts take only what they need.

6
00:00:18,971 --> 00:00:25,613
A PC that needs 300 watts while gaming draws about 300, plus a little lost as heat.

7
00:00:26,363 --> 00:00:31,192
Power supplies are often most efficient somewhere around half of their rated load.

8
00:00:31,472 --> 00:00:34,681
That's one reason a bit of headroom is a good idea.

9
00:00:35,431 --> 00:00:39,567
So a bigger power supply won't raise your power bill much on its own.

10
00:00:39,847 --> 00:00:43,573
Buying one that's far bigger than you need just costs more up front.

11
00:00:43,853 --> 00:00:46,419
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

